Explanation: The comment "@@@ index is either -1 or greater than or equal to 2" refers to the return value of a function called Search. The function may return -1 or a value greater than or equal to 2, so the assert statement asserts that the return value is either -1 or greater than or equal to 2.

The assert statement is constructed using the OLD(s.size) syntax to refer to the previous value of the size variable before the function is called and using the RET variable to refer to the return value of the function.--------------------
